@ConradIrwin A couple of questions on my approach 🙇

1. I only added `Save` and `Overwrite` here because those are the intents used by `:wq` and `:wq!`, respectively. But I noticed there's also `SaveWithoutFormat`, `SaveAll` and `SaveAs`, would it make sense to also check those here?
2. Let me know if this approach makes sense or if you'd rather have me actually prevent the `dirty_project_items_ids` from being updated, something like this:

    ```rust
    // Check if this view has any project items that are not open anywhere else
    // in the workspace, AND that the user has not already been prompted to save.
    // If there are any such project entries, prompt the user to save this item.
    let project = if save_intent != SaveIntent::Save && save_intent != SaveIntent::Overwrite {
        workspace.update(&mut cx, |workspace, cx| {
            ...
            workspace.project().clone()
        })?
    } else {
        workspace.update(&mut cx, |workspace, _| workspace.project().clone())?
    };
    ```

Thank you so much for the help so far! Appreciate it! 

